    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "The implementation is complete and all tests pass.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented idempotent owner creation for `POST /api/owners`: when a create repeats with an already-seen `Idempotency-Key` header, the originally created owner is returned with **200** instead of creating a duplicate.\n\n**How it works** \u2014 the OfficeFloor pipeline gained a first step and a post-save step, following the project's function-injection conventions:\n\n1. **`CheckIdempotency`** (new entry step) \u2014 reads the optional `Idempotency-Key` header via `ServerHttpConnection`. If the key was seen before, it loads the original owner and responds 200 (`ObjectResponse<OwnerDto>`), short-circuiting the pipeline so validation and the duplicate/identity checks never run (they would otherwise 409). Otherwise it takes the `create` flow (`@Flow(\"create\")` \u2192 `validate`) to run the normal create pipeline.\n\n2. **`RecordIdempotency`** (new step after `SaveOwner`) \u2014 once the owner has its generated id, records `key \u2192 ownerId`. Only reached on the create path.\n\n3. **`IdempotencyStore`** \u2014 a `@Component` singleton backed by a `ConcurrentHashMap`, deliberately in-memory (a request-dedup concern, independent of any request's transaction) with first-writer-wins semantics (`putIfAbsent`).\n\nBoth new steps carry `govern: [ transaction ]` like the rest of the pipeline. Absent/blank headers fall straight through to a normal create, so existing behaviour is unchanged.\n\n**Verification** \u2014 `./mvnw -o test` is green: the new `AcceptanceTest.coreIdempotentRepeat` (repeat key returns the same id with 200) passes, and the full suite reports `BUILD SUCCESS` with no failures.",
