    "probe_text": "Here's the complete, in-order trace of `POST /api/owners`. The whole file is wrapped in `govern: [ transaction ]`, so every step below runs in one transaction that commits once at the end (or rolls back on any thrown escalation).\n\n## Gate (before any step)\n- **Authorization** \u2014 `authorize: \"hasRole('OWNER_ADMIN')\"`. Non-admin \u2192 403 (`AuthorizationDeniedException`).\n\n## Ordered pipeline\n\n**1. `CheckIdempotency`** *(side-effect / short-circuit)*\nReads the optional `Idempotency-Key` header. If it names a key already recorded against an existing owner \u2192 responds **200** with that owner and stops (no validation, no duplicate). Otherwise takes the `create` flow.\n\n**2. `ValidateOwnerFields`** \u2014 the validation gate, in this internal order:\n1. *Validation* \u2014 supplied `registrationDate` must not be after the server's today \u2192 `OwnerRegistrationDateFutureException`.\n2. *Validation* \u2014 required, non-blank (collected together, all reported at once): `firstName`, `lastName`, address (composed from `addressLine1`[+`addressLine2`] or legacy flat `address`), `city`, `telephone` \u2192 `OwnerFieldsRequiredException`.\n3. *Validation* \u2014 postcode (optional): must be 4 digits, and if the city maps to a known region (Sydney\u2192NSW, Melbourne\u2192VIC, Brisbane\u2192QLD) must fall in that region's range \u2192 `OwnerPostcodeInvalidException`.\n4. *Side-effect (normalize & republish body)* \u2014 writes back onto the request: normalized `addressLine1`/`addressLine2` and composed `address` (trim/collapse, upper-case, expand ST/RD/AVE); `telephone` \u2192 E.164 (`OwnerTelephoneInvalidException` if it can't form a valid 8\u201315 digit number with matching national length); `email` \u2192 trimmed/lower-cased, with syntax check (`OwnerEmailInvalidException`) and disposable-domain blocklist check (`OwnerEmailDisposableException`). Publishes the body for later steps.\n\n**3. `CheckOwnerDailyLimit`** *(validation)* \u2014 counts existing owners whose `registrationDate` equals the effective business day (supplied-or-today, rolled to a business day); \u2265 **100** \u2192 `OwnerDailyLimitException` (429).\n\n**4. `CheckOwnerCityCapacity`** *(validation)* \u2014 counts existing owners in the same city (case-insensitive); \u2265 **50** \u2192 `OwnerCityCapacityException` (409).\n\n**5. `BuildOwner`** *(side-effect)* \u2014 maps DTO \u2192 `Owner`; defaults `registrationDate` to today if omitted; rolls it forward past weekends/holidays to the next business day.\n\n**6. `AssignHousehold`** *(side-effect)* \u2014 sets `householdId` = first 12 hex of SHA-256(normalized `lastName` `|` `postcode`).\n\n**7. `CheckOwnerIdentityUnique`** *(validation)* \u2014 unless the request set `sharesHousehold=true`, rejects if any **non-deleted** existing owner already has the same `householdId` \u2192 `OwnerIdentityConflictException` (409). (Soft-deleted owners never block.)\n\n**8. `AssignPossibleDuplicate`** *(side-effect)* \u2014 sets `possibleDuplicate=false`/`possibleDuplicateOf=null`; then (unless `sharesHousehold`, and only when a postcode exists) if a non-deleted owner shares `lastName` (case-insensitive) + `postcode` but has a different telephone, flags `possibleDuplicate=true` and `possibleDuplicateOf`= lowest matching id.\n\n**9. `AssignHouseholdSize`** *(side-effect)* \u2014 sets `householdMemberCount` = existing owners sharing `householdId` **+ 1** (the new owner).\n\n**10. `AssignCustomerCode`** *(side-effect)* \u2014 sets `customerCode` = `<REGION>-<HASH8>` (region from postcode; HASH8 from SHA-256 of telephone+lastName), de-duplicated by appending `-2`, `-3`, \u2026 on collision with an existing code.\n\n**11. `AssignNamesakeCount`** *(side-effect)* \u2014 sets `namesakeCount` = existing owners with same `firstName`+`lastName` (case-insensitive), excluding the new one.\n\n**12. `AssignBulkSignupWarning`** *(side-effect)* \u2014 sets `bulkSignupWarning=true` if existing owners on this business day exceed **80**.\n\n**13. `SaveOwner`** *(side-effect)* \u2014 `ownerRepository.save(owner)`; the owner gets its generated id.\n\n**14. `RecordIdempotency`** *(side-effect)* \u2014 if the request carried an `Idempotency-Key`, records key \u2192 new owner id (so a later repeat returns this owner).\n\n**15. `AuditOwnerCreated`** *(side-effect)* \u2014 writes an `AUDIT` log line (id, customerCode, registrationDate, membershipLevel, membershipNumber).\n\n**16. `RespondWithOwnerCreated`** *(side-effect)* \u2014 responds **201 Created** with `Location: /api/owners/{id}` and the `OwnerDto` body.\n\n### Notes on ordering that matter\n- Validation runs **before** the 404/duplicate-style checks by design (invalid body \u2192 400, not masked).\n- Telephone E.164 and email checks happen *after* the required-field check, so a blank telephone is reported as \"required\" rather than \"invalid\".\n- Duplicate detection (steps 7\u20138) runs *after* `householdId` is assigned but *before* `save`, so scans see existing owners only, not the new one.\n- On any escalation thrown, the surrounding transaction rolls back \u2014 nothing is persisted."
